      "supported_finding": "In the target CLI implementation, a parsed positive Retry-After is used only for an already eligible transient HTTP retry, and changes the sleep only when its seconds converted to milliseconds exceed the existing computed sleep. It cannot shorten exponential backoff. When elapsed retry time plus Retry-After exceeds retry-max-time, the CLI exits the retry path instead of scheduling the promised next retry. The candidate describes unconditional override and carries it into the proposed timing evidence.",
